  "clues": [
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its fur is reddish brown on its back and black on its belly and legs.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its long, bushy tail has about 12 red and pale rings.",
      "tags": [
        "long_tail",
        "ringed_tail"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "The soles of its feet are covered in thick fur.",
      "tags": [
        "furry_feet"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It has a 'false thumb', a long wrist bone that helps it grip bamboo.",
      "tags": [
        "false_thumb"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "Bamboo leaves are its main food. It bends the stems down to reach them.",
      "tags": [
        "bamboo_eater"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It sleeps high in the trees and climbs down trunks headfirst.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "habitat",
      "text": "It lives high in the mountains, in forests with thick bamboo underneath.",
      "tags": [
        "high_mountains",
        "bamboo_forest"
      ],
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "conservation",
      "text": "Losing and breaking up its forests is its main threat.",
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its ears are large for its head.",
      "tags": [
        "big_ears"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its colors or pattern help it blend in with its surroundings, so it is hard to see.",
      "tags": [
        "camouflage"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/red-panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It has five claws on each front foot.",
      "tags": [
        "five_front_claws"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It bites or chews with unusual force for its size.",
      "tags": [
        "strong_bite"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/redpanda/characteristics"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Dark lines run from the inner corner of each eye down to its mouth, like tear tracks.",
      "tags": [
        "tear_lines"
      ],
      "source": "smithsonian",
      "url": "https://www.nationalzoo.si.edu/animals/red-panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its fur is mostly red, reddish brown or golden red.",
      "tags": [
        "reddish_fur"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It often rests in the sun to warm its body.",
      "tags": [
        "basker"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/red-panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It makes short, high, bird-like chirping calls.",
      "tags": [
        "chirps"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/red-panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It climbs up big rocks, boulders or cliffs.",
      "tags": [
        "climbs_boulders"
      ],
      "source": "smithsonian",
      "url": "https://www.nationalzoo.si.edu/animals/red-panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It leaves its dung in piles that it comes back to, as messages to others of its kind.",
      "tags": [
        "dung_piles"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2076-2615/11/4/921"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It finds most of its food on the ground.",
      "tags": [
        "feeds_on_ground"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2076-2615/11/4/921"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It makes a loud hissing sound.",
      "tags": [
        "hisses"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/redpanda/behavior"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "Leaves are a main part of its food.",
      "tags": [
        "leaf_eater"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It rests by hanging or perching in tree branches.",
      "tags": [
        "roosts_in_trees"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It spreads plant seeds to new places by eating them, often in fruit, and passing them in its droppings.",
      "tags": [
        "seed_spreader"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It builds a nest or bed of leaves, branches or grass to sleep or rest in.",
      "tags": [
        "sleeping_nests"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "At least sometimes, it stands, rears up, hops or runs on its back legs alone.",
      "tags": [
        "stands_on_hind_legs"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/redpanda/behavior"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It swims well or often.",
      "tags": [
        "swimmer"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/redpanda/behavior"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It defends an area, such as a territory, home patch or den site, against others of its kind.",
      "tags": [
        "territorial"
      ],
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://www.mdpi.com/2076-2615/11/4/921"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It calls with high whistles.",
      "tags": [
        "whistle_calls"
      ],
      "source": "smithsonian",
      "url": "https://www.nationalzoo.si.edu/animals/news/red-panda-bear-and-more-red-panda-facts"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It climbs well or often, in trees, on rocks or both.",
      "tags": [
        "climber"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It sleeps or rests high up in trees.",
      "tags": [
        "sleeps_high_in_trees"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://animals.sandiegozoo.org/animals/red-panda"
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "It isn't a bear or a raccoon. It is the only living member of its own family.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "The giant panda also has a 'false thumb' for bamboo, though the two aren't close relatives.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "There are two kinds, the Himalayan and the Chinese red panda, which split apart about 250,000 years ago.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_panda"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It washes its face with a paw, like a cat.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "life_description",
      "text": "Cubs are born in a hollow tree or a rock crack, mostly in June.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "threat",
      "text": "Its numbers are thought to have fallen by half in 18 years.",
      "source": "iucn"
    }
  ],
